<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine eyes Iranian crude oil supplies for 1997.</title>
<headline>Ukraine eyes Iranian crude oil supplies for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran hopes to supply Ukraine with one million tonnes of crude oil this year and may send more, a Ukrainian energy official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Stepan Yaloveha, spokesman for the State Oil and Gas Committee, said a deal was reached late last month during a Ukrainian delegation's recent visit to Iran.</p>
<p>&quot;Iran is ready to supply Ukraine with four million tonnes of oil annually but the agreement so far is for about one million tonnes,&quot; Yaloveha told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;But some problems remain -- first of all, how to deliver the oil, and how to pay for it.&quot;</p>
<p>Ukraine has been trying to wean itself from Russian crude oil supplies.</p>
<p>Deputy Foreign Minister Kostyantyn Hryshchenko, who headed the Ukrainian delegation, said the Iranian oil would be supplied by tankers and refined at Odessa's oil refinery.</p>
<p>Ukraine's annual oil needs are about 40 million tonnes, three-quarters of which have been supplied by Russia.</p>
<p>-- Rostislav Khotin, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
